{"name":"Ogre Odour","hex":"#fd5240","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ogre","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, grotesque, brutish humanoid monster, typically marked by great strength and a propensity to kill or devour humans.","A cruel person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ogre"},{"term":"odour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["UK standard spelling of odor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/odour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ogre","blocks":[{"text":"An ogre is a legendary monster depicted as a large, hideous, humanoid being that eats ordinary human beings, especially infants and children. Ogres frequently feature in mythology, folklore, and fiction throughout the world. They appear in many classic works of literature, and are most often associated in fairy tales and legend."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Giovanni_Lanfranco_-_Norandino_and_Lucina_Discovered_by_the_Ogre_-_WGA12455.jpg/330px-Giovanni_Lanfranco_-_Norandino_and_Lucina_Discovered_by_the_Ogre_-_WGA12455.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ogre","wikidata":"Q290562"},{"title":"Odor","blocks":[{"text":"An odor or odour is a smell or a scent caused by one or more volatilized chemical compounds generally found in low concentrations that humans and many animals can perceive via their olfactory system. While smell can refer to pleasant and unpleasant odors, the terms scent, aroma, and fragrance are usually reserved for pleasant-smelling odors and are frequently used in the food and cosmetic industry to describe floral scents or to refer to perfumes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Jan_Brueghel_d._O._-_Allegorie_van_de_geur.jpg/330px-Jan_Brueghel_d._O._-_Allegorie_van_de_geur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odor","wikidata":"Q485537"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Puss_in_Boots_%28136548447%29.jpg/500px-Puss_in_Boots_%28136548447%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Puss_in_Boots_%28136548447%29.jpg/1280px-Puss_in_Boots_%28136548447%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Puss_in_Boots_%28136548447%29.jpg/500px-Puss_in_Boots_%28136548447%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Puss in Boots before the ogre. One of the platters on the table serves human babies (illustrated by Gustave Doré).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APuss_in_Boots_(136548447).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Le_Petit_Poucet_%28136548020%29.jpg/500px-Le_Petit_Poucet_%28136548020%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Le_Petit_Poucet_%28136548020%29.jpg/1280px-Le_Petit_Poucet_%28136548020%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Le_Petit_Poucet_%28136548020%29.jpg/500px-Le_Petit_Poucet_%28136548020%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hop-o'-My-Thumb steals the ogre's seven-league boots (illustrated by Gustave Doré, 1862).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALe_Petit_Poucet_(136548020).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Le_Chat_face_%C3%A0_l%27ogre.jpg/120px-Le_Chat_face_%C3%A0_l%27ogre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Le_Chat_face_%C3%A0_l%27ogre.jpg/